{"title":"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(no_coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (no coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a tetrahedron with two isosceles triangle faces with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/49923d7452fdbd88d11f80f7094bb0f823949180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{10}, \\,5\\sqrt{10},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and two isosceles triangle faces with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/29058d1f4d823b0e5104b74fdfedaefece5efde2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{10},\\, 5\\sqrt{10},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e766a44591081fc5b1ee0d9664d0c425551243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> The four vertices of the tetrahedron lie on a sphere with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2e8e8dd78b26ddc9ac278cc179101d30644cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> and the four faces of the tetrahedron are tangent to a sphere with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0001b2ee54d88d0d1930503b5e5e962199c16e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> The distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8cbebf38fa12c5a31ea7748b27b06ebd1c82da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac mn,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f543007c029b5099536028683923f5a1a5e820e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${}m + n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e36d3319de2f03f32326133b1de492a9bbc0189.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(320); pair S = (0, 0); pair A = (0, 110); pair D = (-95, -55); pair C = (95, -55); pair B = (-25, 15); pair R = (0, 25); draw(circle(S, 110), gray+linewidth(0.6)); draw(circle(R, 43), gray+linewidth(0.4)); draw(A--C, black+linewidth(1.1)); draw(A--D, black+linewidth(1.1)); draw(C--D, black+linewidth(1.1)); draw(A--B, dashed+gray+linewidth(0.9)); draw(B--C, dashed+gray+linewidth(0.9)); draw(B--D, dashed+gray+linewidth(0.9)); draw(S--R, dotted+black+linewidth(1.3)); dot(A, p=black+linewidth(4.5)); dot(B, p=black+linewidth(4.5)); dot(C, p=black+linewidth(4.5)); dot(D, p=black+linewidth(4.5)); dot(S, p=red+linewidth(4.5)); dot(R, p=blue+linewidth(4.5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N*3.5); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW*3.0); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE*3.5); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW*3.5); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, S, SW*2.0); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, NE*2.0); label(&quot;$10$&quot;, (A+B)/2, SE); label(&quot;$18$&quot;, (C+D)/2, N); label(&quot;$5\\sqrt{10}$&quot;, (A+D)/2, NW*2.0); label(&quot;$5\\sqrt{10}$&quot;, (B+C)/2, SW); label(&quot;$5\\sqrt{10}$&quot;, (A+C)/2, NE*2.0); label(&quot;$5\\sqrt{10}$&quot;, (B+D)/2, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"498\" height=\"535\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d10dfce2ebf283048c557f6c780bc6e978abe0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import three;size(200,0);currentprojection=orthographic(10,20,15);triple A=(-5,0,0);triple B=(5,0,0);triple C=(0,9,12);triple D=(0,-9,12);triple S=(0,0,25/3);triple R=(0,0,75/16);dot(A,red);dot(B,red);dot(C,red);dot(D,red);dot(S,purple+linewidth(3));dot(R,deepgreen+linewidth(3));label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW);label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE);label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N);label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,-9,12),SW);label(&quot;$S$&quot;,S,E);label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,W);draw(A--B,blue);draw(A--C,blue);draw(B--C,blue);draw(A--D,blue+dashed);draw(B--D,blue);draw(C--D,blue);draw(R--S,red);draw((-10,0,0)--(-5,0,0));draw((5,0,0)--(10,0,0));draw((9,0,0.5)--(10,0,0));draw((9,0,-0.5)--(10,0,0));draw((0,-15,0)--(0,15,0));draw((0,14,0.5)--(0,15,0));draw((0,14,-0.5)--(0,15,0));draw((0,0,0)--(0,0,20));draw((0,0.5,19)--(0,0,20));draw((0,-0.5,19)--(0,0,20));label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(12,0,0),E);label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,16,0),N);label(&quot;$z$&quot;,(0,0,20),N);[/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"435\" />\n</p>\n<div style=\"line-height:2;\">\n<p>We place the tetrahedron in a coordinate system by symmetry:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddeeb1a3641c7eea0b185d29da1d3cc8acdca9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(-5, 0, 0),\\ B(5, 0, 0),\\ C(0, 9, h),\\ D(0, -9, h).\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"18\" />\nGiven <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a96100cff8519ed743ba29097c627cc6c602d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 5\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\nAC^2 &amp;= 5^2 + 9^2 + h^2 = 250, \\\\\nh^2 &amp;= 144 \\implies h = 12.\n\\end{align*}\nSo the vertices are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d18c4a2fbb94451198422198bc3efe671f69ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(-5,0,0),\\ B(5,0,0),\\ C(0,9,12),\\ D(0,-9,12).\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By symmetry, the circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-axis. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bde43bdaac7fb3208eecc1101e39b2c268f732d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=(0,0,a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />.\nUsing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c00aec56db48baaef69b71d18633d364751c0a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SA=SC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nSA^2 &amp;= 25 + a^2, \\\\\nSC^2 &amp;= 81 + (12-a)^2, \\\\\n25 + a^2 &amp;= 225 - 24a + a^2, \\\\\n24a &amp;= 200 \\implies a = \\frac{25}{3}.\n\\end{align*}\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f64f9ed4b50e02b3921694c0ee1081dc4b6340.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\Big(0,0,\\frac{25}{3}\\Big).\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By symmetry, the incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-axis. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acde9585a44f9e09ac7931afebf6d78b14ab3a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=(0,0,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Vectors for plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f42280c37c2184c5096e540b313328926573e93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\quad \\overrightarrow{AC}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\9\\\\12\\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"64\" />\nNormal vector by cross product:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{n}_1 &amp;= \\overrightarrow{AB}\\times\\overrightarrow{AC}\n= \\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&amp;\\mathbf{j}&amp;\\mathbf{k}\\\\10&amp;0&amp;0\\\\5&amp;9&amp;12\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&amp;= \\mathbf{i}(0\\cdot12-0\\cdot9)\n-\\mathbf{j}(10\\cdot12-0\\cdot5)\n+\\mathbf{k}(10\\cdot9-0\\cdot5) \\\\\n&amp;= 0\\mathbf{i}-120\\mathbf{j}+90\\mathbf{k}\n= 30\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\-4\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{align*}\nWe get the equation of the plane:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235043efe6b8212396e4bef0c58acd784eaa9c44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-4y + 3z = 0.\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />\nDistance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798bd8f81850e5ab88cf8997456acbf47bd3dece.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_1 = \\frac{|3b|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^2+3^2}} = \\frac{3|b|}{5}.\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Vectors for plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f34dc67fbea957a660dd1ede0ce467cefc5afa8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\9\\\\12\\end{pmatrix},\\quad \\overrightarrow{AD}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-9\\\\12\\end{pmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"64\" />\nNormal vector by cross product:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{n}_2 &amp;= \\overrightarrow{AC}\\times\\overrightarrow{AD}\n= \\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&amp;\\mathbf{j}&amp;\\mathbf{k}\\\\5&amp;9&amp;12\\\\5&amp;-9&amp;12\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&amp;= \\mathbf{i}(9\\cdot12-12\\cdot(-9))\n-\\mathbf{j}(5\\cdot12-12\\cdot5)\n+\\mathbf{k}(5\\cdot(-9)-9\\cdot5) \\\\\n&amp;= 216\\mathbf{i}-0\\mathbf{j}-90\\mathbf{k}\n= 18\\begin{pmatrix}12\\\\0\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{align*}\nWe get the equation of the plane:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73aa34a67eb7d8041974257d496d49ddb1a1b77b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12x - 5z + 60 = 0.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />\nDistance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72638f33a8f13e566e81fb147e10d6c518f15b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_2 = \\frac{|60-5b|}{\\sqrt{12^2+(-5)^2}} = \\frac{|60-5b|}{13}.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f34963fadbbd2d106228750b133368ad693618f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1=d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{3b}{5} &amp;= \\frac{60-5b}{13}, \\\\\n39b &amp;= 300-25b, \\\\\n64b &amp;= 300 \\implies b = \\frac{75}{16}.\n\\end{align*}\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c083cec24765d5dde7a0ff0af60f644ae42c688.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R=\\Big(0,0,\\frac{75}{16}\\Big).\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Hence, the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is:\n\\begin{align*}\nRS &amp;= \\left|\\frac{25}{3}-\\frac{75}{16}\\right|\n= \\left|\\frac{400-225}{48}\\right|\n= \\frac{175}{48}.\n\\end{align*}\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/69974a96714c78760619d0ec73a58d86960ba38c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(175,48)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae53e943b90fcf7c08c3b920ec01ea8237375c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=175$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b45791b3c5a5e17708d2482627293da9374614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0aaac5063902449175fa1806b003c89ec26e54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m+n = 175+48=\\boxed{223}.\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>~Steven Zheng\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798a6ef213a494d81b4023083909444fd31f4928.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import three;size(200,0);currentprojection=orthographic(10,20,15);triple A=(-5,0,0);triple B=(5,0,0);triple C=(0,21.79,0);triple D=(0,14.35,16.39);dot(A,red);dot(B,red);dot(C,red);dot(D,red);label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW);label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,W);label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E);label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE);draw(A--B,black);draw(A--C,black);draw(B--C,black);draw(A--D,black);draw(B--D,black);draw(C--D,black);label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(A+B)/2,S,blue);label(&quot;$18$&quot;,(C+D)/2,NE,blue);[/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"368\" />\n~Diagram by Confringo\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68caf49f5578223385df388c2a4c199cdfda1953.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(150);pair O=(0,0),C=(15,0),D=(21/5,72/5),DD=(21/5,0),R=(15/4,45/16),RR=(15/4,0),M=(C+D)/2;draw(O--C--D--cycle);draw(D--DD);draw(R--RR);draw(M--O);dot(O);dot(C);dot(D);dot(DD);dot(R);dot(RR);dot(M);label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,SW);label(&quot;$D&#39;$&quot;,DD,SE);label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,NW);label(&quot;$R&#39;$&quot;,RR,S);label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE);label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW);label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,W);label(&quot;$15$&quot;,(O+D)/2,W);label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(O+DD)/2,S);label(&quot;$15-y$&quot;,(C+DD)/2,S);label(&quot;$z$&quot;,(D+DD)/2,E);label(&quot;$18$&quot;,M,NE);draw(Circle(R,45/16),black);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/8012a2637ece93c603dec39c056af0e7f55aec41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(150);pair A=(-5,0);pair O=(0,0);pair B=(5,0);pair C=(0,15);pair SS=(0,7);draw(A--B--C--cycle);draw(C--O);draw(A--SS);dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(O);dot(SS);label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(C+SS)/2,SE);label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(A+SS)/2,SE);label(&quot;$15-x$&quot;,(O+SS)/2,SE);label(&quot;$S&#39;$&quot;,SS,SE);label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE);label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N);label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,S);label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(A+O)/2,S);label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(B+O)/2,S);label(&quot;$10\\sqrt{5}$&quot;,(A+C)/2,NW);label(&quot;$10\\sqrt{5}$&quot;,(B+C)/2,NE);[/asy]\" width=\"178\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Choose face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> as the base. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as the origin, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> along the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> along the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, and the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-axis.\n</p><p>First, find the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Due to the symmetry of the figure, plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77c68f7d7cc94d414b1547e07ed2d170ae319be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a86e649d6411be93866064f4d4a4934a033b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yOz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />-plane. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a058bc8ff053ce285f0fef88b971292d37715a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD&#39; = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/0270fde699188935dd9a686a4852676ce601611a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD&#39; = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />. Then  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b96708c8ae1b4361ce42640461c9869ba959731.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} y^2+z^2=15^2 \\\\ (15-y)^2+z^2=18^2 \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Solving this system yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da194b0a3feac5789ad8dfa21435d0fd2740fbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\dfrac{21}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731d3d62c83ca7706dadf9017b30369f2ff8010b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\dfrac{72}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa8d7c9cfcf54cd17c2f3ce632cdef1424c424a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\left(0,\\dfrac{21}{5},\\dfrac{72}{5}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"116\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Next, find the circumcenter. The center of the circumscribed sphere lies on the line perpendicular to the base through the circumcenter of the base triangle. Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11a1d722d70ee7e8eb11098ff7f3679225c7f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO=\\sqrt{AC^2-AO^2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />. We need a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dd32e2dac59ab16c628510ac3100301f6c3f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CS&#39; = SA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4baf663ec5a09e803a5290b4cd2f78358ebdc0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CS&#39; = AS&#39; = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead9dc10fb9cf2704e930b8d5fc2f8ed95c751a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;O = 15-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />. In right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ead860d13b96fee7e537e65346d04279e6f3136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOS&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />, by the Pythagorean theorem,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716399e64087dea0f724a45e56a6f44160bffdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2=(15-x)^2+5^2,\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />  \nwhich gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7866e5423eeb677b98f82e2986c7b58aed10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43eca6a481ecc0645e676781e82b2773f3402a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OS&#39; = 15-x = \\dfrac{20}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" /> (the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/1953025de24b24f012c163772a845a872cd0c5a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\left(0,\\dfrac{20}{3},h\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"122\" height=\"45\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730bc0c9ed5b49dfe66b0819506c90e45b9125e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS = CS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, so  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40755bf3fe28d76e9be057296c231cea8d0f11f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{25}{3}\\right)^2+h^2}=\\sqrt{(0-0)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{21}{5}-\\dfrac{20}{3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{72}{5}-h\\right)^2}.\\]\" width=\"453\" height=\"53\" />  \nSolving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed30bcf508c8788139652c78e1f64eb7e151f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80b2a83d5cc80a034a9f5cbfcdc1f43aebaad8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\left(0,\\dfrac{20}{3},5\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"121\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Now find the incenter. By volume considerations: connecting each vertex to the incenter divides the tetrahedron into four smaller tetrahedra, each with height equal to the insphere radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and base area equal to the area of a face of the tetrahedron. Their volumes sum to the total volume of the tetrahedron.\n</p><p>The areas of the two types of faces are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff99cacd74b61be0434acb70bce45baec948bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$117$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. The height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606e7cd1c0806551f466e6fbd7bfe5c90c9f957d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_C = \\dfrac{72}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />. Volume equation:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48904454d513b858ceb66f4fd12ced91e5f2682.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot75\\cdot\\dfrac{72}{5}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot(2\\cdot75+2\\cdot117)\\cdot r.\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"38\" />  \nSolving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4053119896646f947049df1f75ab5f362c4112e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\dfrac{45}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/688beb1d23bc01859a5559f20d66d566444998cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_R = \\dfrac{45}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>By symmetry, the incenter also lies in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a86e649d6411be93866064f4d4a4934a033b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yOz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />-plane. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e5279d3f896ef9c6f82885a1936100390b02c000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb2293ddea584456bb9991919b161000a9745c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\angle ROR&#39; = \\dfrac{RR&#39;}{OR&#39;} = \\dfrac{MC}{OM} = \\dfrac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"40\" />. So  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e95a9fdb1d551c36602607f9a8da0706baeb9adb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OR&#39; = \\dfrac43 RR&#39; = \\dfrac43 \\cdot \\dfrac{45}{16} = \\dfrac{15}{4}.\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"38\" />  \nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b9e006cbbbc413f9bb9354b806a577074064e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_R = \\dfrac{15}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80b2a83d5cc80a034a9f5cbfcdc1f43aebaad8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\left(0,\\dfrac{20}{3},5\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"121\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db614925a294357bf2f2cf1ca4e44f3ac4602f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\left(0,\\dfrac{15}{4},\\dfrac{45}{16}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc7287a6547faca8d32afab19c38eeb368758bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{(0-0)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{20}{3}-\\dfrac{15}{4}\\right)^2+\\left(5-\\dfrac{45}{16}\\right)^2}=\\dfrac{175}{48}.\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"53\" />  \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa2c5db610c6d7c961d76200b986305e4f13db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$175$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are coprime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae53e943b90fcf7c08c3b920ec01ea8237375c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=175$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b45791b3c5a5e17708d2482627293da9374614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a6f3a88953118056edcb7695d484ccc02afb52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{223}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Confringo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28no_coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(no_coordinates)\">Solution 3 (no coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (no coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> be the side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Call midpoints of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The faces of our tetrahedron are isosceles triangle so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67c8e84a7b8145439aa10391babf5ced6c623f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=5$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a3acf929a0403471a4d69df974f0a6cf9da1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, along with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db559baf38b57282935f2efe2dff62f54fb59b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN\\perp AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f1cfbefbedbfd561507994462238d928bea1943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN\\perp CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />. By symmetry we know both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> locate on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794436117d3f4e3d8b5c78b9dce5f01be7b40810.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import olympiad; size(150);pair M=(0,0),C=(15,0),D=(21/5,72/5),R=(15/4,45/16),E=(15/4,0),N=(C+D)/2;draw(M--C--D--cycle);draw(R--E);draw(M--N);dot(M);dot(C);dot(D);dot(R);dot(E);dot(N);label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,SW);label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,NW);label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S);label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE);label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW);label(&quot;$N$&quot;,N,W);label(&quot;$15$&quot;,(M+D)/2,W);label(&quot;$18$&quot;,N,NE);label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(M+R)/2,S);label(&quot;$12-x$&quot;,(R+N)/2,SE);draw(rightanglemark(M,N,C,30),red);draw(rightanglemark(R,E,C,30),red);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>For the position of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c5299463a89b00f300cbc21d9f2be9ded88f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MR=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. By isosceles we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e63ca8c2e3b50bf96b79205191fda60276949553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM\\perp AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> so the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a3616fad4fb1a37aedeca8f3ddb890169f5ac3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to the place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the plance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />. The same happens for the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />. In the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a55f53683866d6bdc726eb3e3f7c9da9a20307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM=\\sqrt{25\\cdot 10-25}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"207\" height=\"21\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d594add03a9f408fb2ccf21f650e4661e0f3a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=\\sqrt{15^2-9^2}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" /> in the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3f7db9e5618aa83bb58ddccac7693cf92a75d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CMD$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Draw altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and call the foot as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c009207e19c9e475110e51a18b423d7f59f85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MRE\\sim \\triangle MCN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3ef1666450f339b93c9ce4c494d160b86d7d8ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RE=\\dfrac{3}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f39d3f6da95fa66928b7a68e766f47a00425b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, we also use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cbcb0b248e894d1613038099a69d9106c60f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RN=12-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and similar triangles to get the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7b12b86e7afe9b1c44c0a02c8ed4becbf105944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5}{13}(12-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />. The two distances are equal so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d575604131226e6e98c39300af2f5c455961141e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{5}x=\\dfrac{5}{13}(12-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a96bc593ec67da8e8bff3e2c2e2ac1289597558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MR=x=\\dfrac{75}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1bbfbeeb72f70537941221eb764829e7ff50fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(150);pair A=(-5,0);pair O=(0,0);pair B=(5,0);pair C=(0,15);pair SS=(0,7);draw(A--B--C--cycle);draw(C--O);draw(A--SS);dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(O);dot(SS);label(&quot;$12-y$&quot;,(C+SS)/2,SE);label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW);label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(O+SS)/2,SE);label(&quot;$S$&quot;,SS,SE);label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE);label(&quot;$N$&quot;,C,N);label(&quot;$M$&quot;,O,S);label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(A+O)/2,S);label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(B+O)/2,S);draw(rightanglemark(C,O,A,30),red);[/asy]\" width=\"182\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>For the position of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2022d047376827debe8d67777371f11ba43bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MS=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0b01aaf32688cd96864a460fb4d52dde3ee296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0c273100e41f0053eb5ccfeeed2f7d41135f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS=\\sqrt{25+y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"24\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e97ca4a90c04930b31b03af3d2180ffbf86467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CNS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbf2c572650a2ed7316ffa64410f2655db77fbed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CS=\\sqrt{(12-y)^2+9^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"35\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e40eaed9b66e6d69ac2ef4e9fd6903f4c182933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS=CS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> we solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/37805df581982f474d3d00e018df6ceaa1c89f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MS=y=\\dfrac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>In summary, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0f029483d18da17b816c6bd8e375194b0f10a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS=MS-MR=\\dfrac{25}{3}-\\dfrac{75}{16}=\\dfrac{175}{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"286\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a6f3a88953118056edcb7695d484ccc02afb52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{223}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~figures are based on the ones from Confringo.\n</p><p>~lanouzhihun\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II\" title=\"2026 AIME II\">2026 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•